{
    maps_state_dir = "state"
    maps_state_dir = ${?MAPS_STATE_DIR}
    include "registries/aaosa_basic.hocon"

    metadata = {
        description = "The watcher network. Owns mid-episode strategic analysis WITHIN the current episode. The runner invokes this network every N successful steps (kind=periodic) — i.e. at steps 10,20,...,90 of the 100-step episode. It reads the cumulative per-episode telemetry and logs actionable trials so the game-runner's specialists can act on them next turn. End-of-episode close-out and whole-run synthesis live in the separate planner network.",
        tags = ["maps", "industry", "consultant", "micro", "advisor"],
        sample_queries = [
            "kind=periodic episode=1 step=20 cumulative_reward=1500 final_reward=null",
            "kind=periodic episode=1 step=90 cumulative_reward=42000 final_reward=null"
        ]
    },

    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    max_steps = 4000,
    max_execution_seconds = 12000,

    tools = [
        {
            name = "mid_episode_analyst",
            function = ${inquiry_call} {
                description = "Mid-episode analyzer (kind=periodic), invoked every 10 steps: diagnoses the live profit trajectory against the best episode, logs its own micro trials, prunes the ones not working, and returns an actionable advisory for the player's next turn."
            },
            instructions = """
You analyze the current live game state at mid-episode.
GOAL: name the MAIN issues holding this run back and design targeted micro trials that fix them.

You are the only part of this harness that can correct the episode WHILE it is still running.
The episode-start plan cannot revise itself; you get roughly nine looks at the run, one every ten steps,
to steer it toward more profit. Always cite evidence (step + metric) from telemetry. Never use outside knowledge.

## Procedures:

1. Gather context:
    - `scratchpad`: the note left by you for yourself at the last check-in, 10 steps ago
    - `EpisodeTelemetry()`: every step so far in the current episode.
    - `state_read('status_full')`: the complete park AS IT STANDS RIGHT NOW.
    - `RunTelemetry(select='best')`: the best episode run, for reference only.
    - `ActiveTrials()`: the macro and micro trials now running, with their criteria.
    - `state_read('trial_strategies_outcome')`: past outcomes. Do NOT revisit a failed trial.

2. Micro trials:
   - Review ONLY micro trials from the `ActiveTrials()` result already gathered above. Drop any that are unproductive, failed, or obsolete with `DeleteTrial(trial_id)`.
   - Diagnose the live blocker: cash piled up while research never triggered; a high-value asset unlocked but
    unplaced, underbuilt, unreachable, or earning $0; a shop out_of_service; a ride with low uptime; or other
    directly evidenced drag. Design the fixes.
   - If the park is leaving an unlocked lever unused, propose a trial that pushes it harder.
   - Propose however many new micro trials the current evidence justifies; there is no fixed numerical cap.
    Each is small, concrete, new, falsifiable, and explicit about action, condition, metric, and trigger phase.
    Put them in different domains, repeat neither macro direction nor any failed trial, and point them along the
    macro strategy. Save each with `LogTrial`.

3. LAST: if the NEXT check-in must know something, usually a drag being watched, call `scratchpad(note=...)` otherwise skip.

4. Return a concise actionable advisory for the player's next turn.

Notes: never extrapolate beyond current telemetry or use outside knowledge. Micro trials must never bankrupt
the park or sacrifice compounding investments for a short-term gain.
""",
            middleware = [
                {"class": "middleware.trim_history_middleware.TrimHistoryMiddleware", "args": {}}
                {"class": "middleware.static_prompt_caching_middleware.StaticPromptCachingMiddleware", "args": {"ttl": "1h"}}
            ],
            tools = ["state_read", "EpisodeTelemetry", "RunTelemetry", "ActiveTrials", "LogTrial", "DeleteTrial", "scratchpad"]
        },

        {
            name = "scratchpad",
            class = "coded_tools.scratchpad.Scratchpad",
            function = {
                description = "Private memo for this network; player and planner hold their own. An omitted or empty note reads and clears the note left at your last check-in; a non-empty note leaves up to 5 lines for the next one. Writes replace; no history is kept.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        note = {
                            type = "string",
                            description = "Up to 5 lines to carry into your NEXT run only. Omit or pass an empty string to read-and-clear instead."
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            args = { pad = "watcher" }
        },

        {
            name = "RunTelemetry",
            class = "coded_tools.run_telemetry.RunTelemetry",
            function = {
                description = "With select='best', returns the highest-scoring episode across all runs as raw per-step rows, unaggregated — your yardstick for pace. Excludes the in-flight run, and returns empty when no prior episode exists.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        select = { type = "string", description = "Pass 'best' to get the best-ever episode as raw filtered steps." }
                    }
                }
            }
        },

        {
            name = "EpisodeTelemetry",
            class = "coded_tools.episode_telemetry.EpisodeTelemetry",
            function = {
                description = "Per-step record for ONE episode, read from run.jsonl: {steps, rejections, rollup}, exists=false before any row is written. Each step carries its full action args and metrics; `rejections` records every action the sim refused, booked as a wait with the original action and error.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        episode   = { type = "int", description = "Episode number to read. Omit to use the latest episode present in the log." }
                        from_step = { type = "int", description = "Only return steps >= this (mid-episode tail). Omit for the full episode." }
                    }
                }
            }
        },

        {
            name = "LogTrial",
            class = "coded_tools.log_trial.LogTrial",
            function = {
                description = "Mints a collision-free trial_id and appends the paired lines: the one-line rule to trial_strategies, the metadata and success/failure criteria to trial_strategies_criteria. Use it for every new trial: it owns id minting and criteria formatting, and takes origin from this network's config.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        episode           = { type = "int", description = "Current episode number." }
                        step_start        = { type = "string",  description = "Step at which the trial activates (as a string), or the literal 'end_of_episode'." }
                        domain            = { type = "string",  description = "One of: rides, shops, staff, research, layout, survey, coordinator." }
                        section           = { type = "string",  description = "Target playbook section header (or 'new')." }
                        edit_type         = { type = "string",  description = "'add_line' or 'replace_line'." }
                        new_text          = { type = "string",  description = "The one-line rule to add/replace (no rationale or metrics embedded)." }
                        find_text         = { type = "string",  description = "replace_line only: the exact existing playbook line to replace." }
                        rationale         = { type = "string",  description = "One sentence citing step(s) / metric delta." }
                        success_criterion = { type = "string",  description = "Observable metric + direction + evaluation window (turns; fits in the fixed 100-step episode)." }
                        failure_criterion = { type = "string",  description = "Observable metric that would falsify the trial." }
                    }
                    required = ["episode", "step_start", "domain", "section", "edit_type", "new_text", "rationale", "success_criterion", "failure_criterion"]
                }
            }
            args = { origin = "micro" }
        },

        {
            name = "DeleteTrial",
            class = "coded_tools.delete_trial.DeleteTrial",
            function = {
                description = "Removes ONE micro trial mid-episode once it is unproductive or obsolete. Accepts micro trial_ids, as listed by ActiveTrials(trial_origin='micro'). Deletes the paired lines from trial_strategies and trial_strategies_criteria. Writes no OUTCOME line — micro trials are episode-scoped and are not ledgered.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        trial_id = { type = "string", description = "The micro trial_id to delete (e.g. 't3_2'), taken from ActiveTrials(trial_origin='micro')." }
                    }
                    required = ["trial_id"]
                }
            }
        },

        {
            name = "ActiveTrials",
            class = "coded_tools.active_trials.ActiveTrials",
            function = {
                description = "Returns the trials in force this episode, joining the rule body from trial_strategies with the metadata and criteria from trial_strategies_criteria. Filter by domain and/or trial_origin ('micro'|'macro'); omit both for all active trials.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        domain = { type = "string", description = "Filter to one domain: rides, shops, staff, research, layout, survey or coordinator. Omit for all domains." }
                        trial_origin = { type = "string", description = "Filter to 'micro' or 'macro'; omit for both. Named trial_origin, not origin — the framework injects a reserved 'origin' key that would silently override it." }
                    }
                }
            }
        },

        {
            name = "state_read",
            class = "coded_tools.state_read.StateRead",
            function = {
                description = "Read a file by its logical name from the operator-configured name_map.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        name = {
                            type = "string",
                            description = "Logical name of the file to read; must be one the operator mapped in name_map.",
                            enum = ["status_full", "trial_strategies_outcome"]
                        }
                    },
                    required = ["name"]
                }
            },
            args = {
                max_content_chars = 120000
                name_map = {
                    # The LIVE park, refreshed by the game-runner's ParkStatus every
                    # turn. Telemetry rows carry only aggregates (num_rides, park_value),
                    # so these are the analyst's ONLY view of which asset is the drag and
                    # which tier is already unlocked. Read, never written, from here.
                    status_full                 = ${maps_state_dir}"/status_full.json"
                    trial_strategies_outcome    = ${maps_state_dir}"/trial_strategies_outcome.md"
                }
            }
        },
    ]
}
